{"id":"56","title":"Home","goal":"Recognize selected housing, room and furniture terms and use them to describe a place or need.","language":"en","study":[{"id":"56-study-0","title":"Start here","blocks":[{"id":"ch56-b0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"This vocabulary supports Chapters 57–64. Start with your own setting or one practice home; use the other words as a reference."}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":6,"ja":"","theme":"home-vocabulary"},{"id":"56-study-1","title":"Types of homes and areas","blocks":[{"id":"ch56-b1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"An "},{"text":"apartment","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a home within a building containing other spaces or homes. A "},{"text":"house","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a residential building. A "},{"text":"duplex","emphasis":true},{"text":" can refer to a building divided into two homes in the American housing sense used here. A "},{"text":"townhouse","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a house joined to others in a row. A "},{"text":"cabin","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a small, often simple house, associated with places such as rural or vacation settings."}],"span":[10,10],"phraseIds":["ch56-p281016596872988","ch56-p101217596824895","ch56-p144558074325428","ch56-p160453013627435","ch56-p190050587016647"]},{"id":"ch56-b2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"neighborhood","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the surrounding local area. "},{"text":"Upstairs","emphasis":true},{"text":" and "},{"text":"downstairs","emphasis":true},{"text":" describe higher and lower levels. A "},{"text":"basement","emphasis":true},{"text":" is below or partly below ground level. In U.S. building numbering, "},{"text":"first floor","emphasis":true},{"text":" usually refers to the ground-level floor. Check the signs in a particular building rather than assuming every numbering scheme is identical."}],"span":[12,12],"phraseIds":["ch56-p67154648938384","ch56-p72316940920025","ch56-p166161735522562","ch56-p267658747322233","ch56-p24427264458818"]}],"line":8,"ja":"","theme":"home-vocabulary"},{"id":"56-visual","title":"Look & understand","widget":"home","blocks":[]},{"id":"56-study-2","title":"Rooms and parts","blocks":[{"id":"ch56-b3","type":"table","header":[[{"text":"Word"}],[{"text":"Meaning"}]],"rows":[[[{"text":"bedroom"}],[{"text":"room used for sleeping"}]],[[{"text":"bathroom"}],[{"text":"room with a toilet and sink, often also a bathtub or shower"}]],[[{"text":"kitchen"}],[{"text":"space for preparing food"}]],[[{"text":"living room"}],[{"text":"shared room for relaxing or spending time together"}]],[[{"text":"dining room"}],[{"text":"room used for meals"}]],[[{"text":"hallway"}],[{"text":"passage connecting rooms"}]],[[{"text":"laundry room"}],[{"text":"space for washing clothes"}]],[[{"text":"garage"}],[{"text":"space for a vehicle or other storage"}]],[[{"text":"balcony"}],[{"text":"outside platform attached to a building"}]],[[{"text":"yard"}],[{"text":"outdoor land beside or around a home"}]]],"span":[16,27],"phraseIds":["ch56-p176722265599316","ch56-p205000862482462","ch56-p237970842512364","ch56-p158949364003442","ch56-p118054724320314","ch56-p177933545725294","ch56-p22835058029473","ch56-p50632897849290","ch56-p20368596916535","ch56-p260238287607387"],"phraseCells":[["ch56-p176722265599316",null],["ch56-p205000862482462",null],["ch56-p237970842512364",null],["ch56-p158949364003442",null],["ch56-p118054724320314",null],["ch56-p177933545725294",null],["ch56-p22835058029473",null],["ch56-p50632897849290",null],["ch56-p20368596916535",null],["ch56-p260238287607387",null]]},{"id":"ch56-b4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Roof","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"fence","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"stairs","emphasis":true},{"text":", and "},{"text":"front door","emphasis":true},{"text":" identify useful parts of a home. A "},{"text":"home office","emphasis":true},{"text":" is space used for working at home."}],"span":[29,29],"phraseIds":["ch56-p1529